    "lawCode": "Amd §202, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S1753\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the elder law, in relation to requiring the state office for\nthe aging to review programs addressing the needs of the aging veteran\npopulation\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nRequires the director of the New York State Office for the Aging\n(NYSOFA) to periodically review the programs offered by NYSOFA to\nensure that they are appropriately responding to the needs of New\nYork State's Military Veterans population.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. Amends the Elder Law, Section 202, by adding a new\nsubdivision 15. Requires the director, in consultation with the\ndirector of the division of veteran's affairs, to periodically review\nprograms operated by NYSOFA to ensure that the needs of the State's\naging veteran population are being met and to develop improvements to\nprograms to meet those needs.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nElder Law; Article 2, Programs for the Elderly; Title 1, State Office\nfor the Aging; Section 202, General Powers and Duties of Office\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nNew York State has the second largest population of military veterans\nin the nation. Many of New York's veterans proudly served in World\nWar II, Korea, and Vietnam. Because of the high concentration of\nveterans that participated in these conflicts, New York's veteran\npopulation is highly concentrated with people approaching and over\nthe age of 60. At this time, many of these people are accessing NYSOFA\n programs, however there is no requirement that these programs be\nspecifically tailored or responsive to the needs and desires of New\nYork's Veterans. This bill would require the NYSOFA director and the\ndirector of the division of veteran's affairs to collaborate and\nreview NYSOFA programs to ensure that they are catering to the needs\nof New York's veterans.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2011:      Senate-New Bill/A.544-Referred to Aging\n2009-10: A.11225 - Passed Assembly\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
